WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
One concept's life.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.833
You ask a question, and Gemini answers it, directly or Socratically.

3
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:16.133
Gemini also extracts the concept you learned, as JSON, and the tutor stores it with a streak and a last grade.

4
00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:21.733
The reinforcement learning agent looks at that state and picks how long to wait.

5
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:28.500
When the concept is due, the tutor interrupts you with a recall check. Nobody asked it to.

6
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.800
Gemini grades your answer zero, one or two.

7
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:38.933
The grade and the days you actually waited become the reward. One Q update, and a new gap.

8
00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:44.533
Then the loop repeats, and each time the agent knows you a little better.

9
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:55.200
Learning from scratch on one person would take months. So the agent pre-trains on simulated students, then keeps learning from your real grades.

10
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:02.333
It works because the live tutor uses the same eighteen states and the same reward as the simulator.

11
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:10.233
And for demos, one line in the env file makes a tutor day last one minute. Now go build yours.

